From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 04:01:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/11] docs: describe resource updates, pagination and the API
 contract

The CHANGELOG, README and module mapping did not mention the new PUT
and PATCH endpoints, list pagination, the server-owned generation, the
derived decision risk level or the contract drift test, and the README
had no section describing the REST API.

The 1.1.0 CHANGELOG lists the additions, marks the breaking changes
(server-owned generation, strict create, signed registry page tokens,
derived risk level) and records the fixes. The README gains a REST API
section with the endpoint table, the update and pagination rules, an
example, and what an update does not do yet: the controller does not
redeploy on a spec change, and a change submitted after the deployment
workflow started does not take effect although observedGeneration
catches up. The module mapping lists the new modules, the new tests and
the registry_meta table.
